{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pulls/4938","id":4817656385,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJphPqM8AAAABHyeaQQ","html_url":"https://github.com/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pull/4938","diff_url":"https://github.com/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pull/4938.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pull/4938.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/issues/4938","number":4938,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Preserve source evidence while repairing default RO-Crate routes","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The default semantic TSV emits obsolete Dataset keys, sends documentary strings into object-valued fields, and turns some source predicates into stronger unsupported claims. This change defines fourteen routes: construct supported whole narratives, retain declined assertions outside Dataset, and accept byte counts only from an explicit nonnegative integer source.\n\nBoth builders, mergers, CLI/API adapters and batch publishers retain mandatory route evidence and prepare a bound sidecar. Evidence preserves missing/null/false distinctions, complete source text, list order and duplicates, original and processed occurrences, source pointers, exact mapping bytes and generated-input lifetimes. Supplemental root assertions have a separate report section, with their actual construction/decline disposition. API construction counts follow renamed output slots while retaining the historical TSV denominator and diagnostic identities. Publication preserves Dataset validation and per-file atomicity.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The actual Codex adversarial plugin approved final commit `00b80002371fe119bc089445234d6b2f5bd5e24d` with no material findings.\n- 2,273 tests passed on each genuine Python 3.13 and 3.9 runtime, including 423 new cases; ordered collections match, with zero failures/errors/skips and source inventories/pins preserved.\n- Real packaged/hidden CLI publication and API regressions cover supplemental exact-size values, absent/null/false values, reordered root/member graphs, aliases, deferred routes, custom maps and full sidecar recovery. The three selected new regressions failed on the previous production code and passed after correction. The original failed baseline wrapper is retained; a separate checked classifier confirms those exact semantic failures with 33 controls.\n- The retained five-input comparison, executed before the final reporting/count corrections, covers two builders and two graph orders: all 20 candidate records had zero Dataset errors and passed saved-byte preparation, versus 172 error occurrences and 4 accepted baseline records. Complete outputs, source evidence and all 40 preparation gates were compared.\n- Non-target values and ordered errors were preserved in that comparison. Both scorers retained complete score dictionaries, ties, order and primary selection; all 81 historical ranking tuples stayed unchanged. Current regressions also preserve that ranking contract.\n- The construction comparison passed 30 schema controls and 56 classifier controls. Earlier failed harness attempts retain their original identities.\n\nThese are software-validation results. Construction and evidence accounting do not establish improved source coverage, scientific truth, `exactMatch` or no loss. Fresh output publication and figure/comparison obligations remain under #2915, #4594 and #4385; keep those parents open.\n\nImplementation for #4932. Keep #4932 open through the five-input publication tracked under #4594.\nCloses #4934.\nCloses #4935.\nCloses #4936.\nCloses #4937.\nCloses #4939.\nCloses #4940.\nCloses #4941.\nCloses #4942.\n","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:15:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T09:57:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-11T09:57:29Z","merged_at":"2026-10-11T09:57:29Z","merge_commit_sha":"ffc4ca922723caa620af2e32a31ad538bc5a5ac9","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pulls/4938/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pulls/4938/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/issues/4938/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bridge2ai/data-sheets-schema/statuses/00b80002371fe119bc089445234d6b2f5bd5e24d","head":{"label":"bridge2ai:fix/4932-legacy-route-dispositions","ref":"fix/4932-legacy-route-dispositions","sha":"00b80002371fe119bc089445234d6b2f5bd5e24d","user":{"login":"bridge2ai","id":103535911,"node_id":"O_kgDOBivVJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103535911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bridge2ai","html_url":"https://github.com/bridge2ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bridge2ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bridge2ai/following{/other_user}","gist